// toplevel-anon-fn-parse-errors.ta — a bare anonymous `fn(...)` at top level
// has no binding target, so it must be rejected with a parse error (it used
// to be silently mis-parsed as `(define (nil) ...)` with params/annotations
// dropped). Anonymous lambdas in expression position remain valid:
// `let f = fn(x) -> int { x };` still parses (see parser-ast.ta).
fn(x) { x }
fn(x) -> int { x }
fn(x, y) -> int { x + y }
fn { 42 }
pub fn(x) { x }